# Force LF line endings on text files that get exec'd or parsed by Linux tools
# inside containers, regardless of the host platform's core.autocrlf setting.
#
# Background: this repo has core.autocrlf=true (set on at least one developer's
# machine), which silently rewrote LF→CRLF on Windows checkouts. Once a CRLF
# data-server/start.sh was COPY'd into the data container, /bin/bash refused
# to exec it because the shebang line ended with `\r`. The data container
# entered a Restart loop and HudObserver POSTs to data:8088 timed out.
#
# These rules pin per-file-type EOLs so the issue can't recur regardless of
# host or autocrlf setting.

*.sh                       text eol=lf
data-server/Dockerfile     text eol=lf
data-server/supervisord.conf text eol=lf
*.yml                      text eol=lf
*.yaml                     text eol=lf
Dockerfile                 text eol=lf
Makefile                   text eol=lf
